Wording and tables of the CLP Regulation
----------------------------------------

The package carries the German wording of the hazard, precautionary and
supplemental statements (src/sdb_reader/clp_statements_de.json) and the tables
that give the pictograms and the signal word of a hazard statement
(src/sdb_reader/pictograms.py).

Source: Regulation (EC) No 1272/2008 of the European Parliament and of the
Council of 16 December 2008 on classification, labelling and packaging of
substances and mixtures (OJ L 353, 31.12.2008, p. 1), consolidated version of
1 July 2026, German (CELEX 02008R1272-20260701), as published by the
Publications Office of the European Union. The tools under tools/clp/ fetch
that text, take the statements from it and check the tables against it.

The consolidated text says of itself that it serves information only and has
no legal effect; binding are the texts published in the Official Journal of
the European Union.

Reuse: Commission Decision 2011/833/EU of 12 December 2011 on the reuse of
Commission documents (OJ L 330, 14.12.2011, p. 39; CELEX 32011D0833), which
covers documents published by the Publications Office on the Commission's
behalf, makes them "available for reuse ... for commercial or non-commercial
purposes" (Article 4) and names as conditions "the obligation for the reuser
to acknowledge the source of the documents" and "the obligation not to distort
the original meaning or message of the documents" (Article 6(2)).
